## Docker Image Configuration
## GitHub Container Registry image (defaults to ghcr.io/${GITHUB_OWNER}/golang-proxy:latest)
## IMPORTANT: Set GITHUB_OWNER to the repository owner (organization name or username), not your personal username
## This should match the owner of the GitHub repository where images are pushed
## Set GOLANG_PROXY_IMAGE to override the full image path, or set GITHUB_OWNER to use default format
GITHUB_OWNER=repository-owner-or-org-name
# GOLANG_PROXY_IMAGE=ghcr.io/repository-owner-or-org-name/golang-proxy:latest

## Debug Mode
DEBUG=false

## Proxy Configuration - Comma-separated list of allowed domains
ALLOWED_DOMAINS=pzero-sfdc-server:3000,localhost:3000

## CORS Configuration - Allowed origin(s) for cross-origin requests
## Can be a single origin (e.g., http://localhost:1420) or comma-separated list
## Use "*" to allow all origins (not recommended for production)
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:1420

## Environment (development/production) - affects error message detail
ENVIRONMENT=development

## Cookie Domain - Domain to use for Set-Cookie headers in proxy responses
## If set, all Set-Cookie headers from proxied responses will have their domain overridden
COOKIE_DOMAIN=proxy.ziti
